# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
build
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
# Every real env file, not just `.env` exactly - `.env.local`, `.env.atlas` and
# friends carry credentials just as happily. The example is the one exception.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
prod.env
# Private keys and tokens, however they land in a working copy.
*.pem
*.key
token*.json
yarn.lock
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# The rest of the secrets-and-keys block the sibling repos carry. A scan before
# pushing found this repo was missing these four while the backend and the front
# had them: `check-ignore id_rsa` here returned nothing, so a key file with no
# extension would have staged. Nothing of the sort exists in this tree today --
# the point is that it can no longer arrive by accident in the one of the three
# repos that was not covered.
secrets/
*.p12
*credentials*.json
id_rsa
